From: j7 fb
Subject: j7: do not print a crash report for a SIGKILLed spawn

j7nospawn stops bluetoothd and fairplayd.H2 from running, but every refused
exec leaves a process that the spawn machinery kills with SIGKILL, and the
console crash reporter dumps its registers and a backtrace each time. Those
registers belong to the image that never loaded, so the report says nothing.
The console is the 115200-baud UART, so a few dozen lines per attempt costs
more than the attempt itself - the 2026-11-14 log is dominated by it.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/exception.c b/osfmk/kern/exception.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/exception.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/exception.c
@@ -843,6 +843,19 @@
 	arm_saved_state_t *ss = find_user_regs(thread);
 	uint64_t slide = 0, mh = task->mach_header_vm_address;
 
+	/*
+	 * A process killed with SIGKILL and no signal code has no fault to
+	 * report: the registers it would print belong to the image it failed to
+	 * become. On this phone that is exactly the spawn machinery tearing down
+	 * a refused exec, and the 2026-11-14 log spends most of its console on
+	 * it - a few dozen lines per attempt, over the 115200-baud UART, while
+	 * SpringBoard is waiting for the CPU. Skip that case and keep the report
+	 * for real faults.
+	 */
+	if (sig == 9 /* SIGKILL */ && code == 0) {
+		return;
+	}
+
 	vm_shared_region_t sr = vm_shared_region_get(task);
 	if (sr != NULL) {
 		slide = sr->sr_slide;
